-> Reference: modules — `link <path> [as <alias>]` brings a file's public
-> bindings and handlers into scope. With an alias, they're reached as
-> `alias.name`/`emit ... to alias`; without one, they're flattened into
-> the current scope directly (see the Modules guide section).
link module-helper as m
assert m.double = 42

emit Square { side = 4 } to m get sq
assert sq.area = 16
